    "result_text": "All 45 tests pass, including every identity-related checkpoint (Cp09, Cp14, Cp16, Cp17, Cp21, Cp30, Cp31, Cp32). The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and every value derived from it follows.\n\n**New: `CustomerCodes` helper** (`rest/function/common/CustomerCodes.java`)\n- `of(Owner)` builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where `REGION` = `Localities.of(postcode, city)` (postcode range preferred, city fallback, else `UNKNOWN`) and `HASH8` = first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`.\n- `hash8(...)` computes the digest over UTF-8 bytes.\n- `localityOf(Owner)` reads the region straight off the customer code (the identity is now the single source), falling back to `Localities.of(...)` only when the code hasn't been assigned yet.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 dropped the per-city sequence logic and the `OwnerRepository` dependency entirely; now just sets `CustomerCodes.of(owner)`. The telephone is already E.164-normalized at this point, so the hash is stable.\n\n**`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 `locality` now derives from the region-and-hash identity via `CustomerCodes.localityOf(owner)` instead of recomputing independently.\n\n**Automatically carried over** (they read `customerCode`): the membership number (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), its Luhn check digit, and the create audit line \u2014 all now reflect the new identity.\n\nStale javadoc referencing the old `SYD-SMI-0007` format was updated across `AssignMembershipNumber`, `CheckDigits`, and `RejectCityAtCapacity`.",
